  "s6": {
    "duration": 30.625,
    "text": "Now, here's what you'll do in this first module. You'll work with two small, made-up pictures of the same sky, one reference and one target. You'll start by looking at what a picture is made of. Then you'll find every way the two pictures differ, and work out a plan to keep only the real changes in the sky. You'll finish by meeting the cuPhoton stages that carry out your plan. You won't write any code, and there's no real telescope data yet. Your tutor is an AI agent: it does the typing, and you do the thinking.",
